ichard Hudson (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Richard Hudson seeks another term in North Carolina's 9th District against Democrat Richard Ojeda. The district leans Republican by about eight points, and Hudson carries the usual incumbent advantages. Ten of eleven expert ratings call the race Likely R, with one rating it Solid R and one Lean R, and prediction markets give Hudson roughly a 98 percent chance of winning.\n\nOjeda has raised nearly $3 million, making this one of the cycle's most expensive House races, but he enters the final stretch with under $50,000 on hand while Hudson retains about $926,000. Two Democratic-sponsored polls from September and October show Hudson ahead by four points, closer than the district's lean would suggest. Early-voting reports from Cumberland County have given Democrats some hope, but the overall evidence still favors Hudson by a solid margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0964, "margin": -7.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1187, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1157, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1153, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0919, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.09, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1101, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1255, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1701, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1283, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1244, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1166, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1479, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.13, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1287, "margin": -6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1426, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1099, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0748, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -8.5}, {